uptime - displays time elapsed since system startup

Description:
The 'uptime' command retrieves and displays the amount of time that has elapsed
since the system was started. The kernel reports uptime in milliseconds (PIT
tick resolution); the command converts this to a human-readable format with
years, months, days, hours, minutes, and seconds as appropriate. Durations under
one second are shown in milliseconds.

Usage:
uptime

Examples:
uptime
